Third-party and source materials
--------------------------------

1. Sanskrit base texts. The stotras published here are ancient
   compositions in the public domain. The Śrī Durgā Saptaślokī is a
   selection from the Durgā Saptaśatī (Devī Māhātmya) of the
   Mārkaṇḍeya Purāṇa.

2. Electronic transcriptions. The romanized text of the Śrī Durgā
   Saptaślokī was keyed from shlokam.org, which states no license for
   its transcription. See SOURCES.md §1.2 for the full provenance
   statement, the licensing analysis, and the resulting block on
   commercial redistribution. Every correction, normalization, and
   emendation applied to the received text is logged in SOURCES.md
   §§1.3–1.6.

3. Fonts. Latin/IAST and Devanāgarī use fonts already present on the
   reader's operating system; none are bundled or fetched for those.
   Telugu is set in Baloo Tammudu 2, embedded in the Śrī Durgā
   Saptaślokī page as a subsetted woff2. It is licensed under the SIL
   Open Font License 1.1 (© 2019 The Baloo 2 Project Authors); the
   license text is vendored at fonts/BalooTammudu2-OFL.txt. The OFL
   permits this embedding and its distribution as part of this work.
   See SOURCES.md §2.

4. Bundled code. teltools.js — the maintainer's own transliteration
   library from github.com/revurpk/teltools — is inlined into the
   Śrī Durgā Saptaślokī page to render the Devanāgarī and Telugu
   scripts from the IAST source. It remains under its own Apache
   License 2.0 (© 2026 Pradyumna Revur) and is not relicensed. It is
   embedded in the page, never fetched from a network. See SOURCES.md
   §§1.8, 3.

